AIM - To implement Multi Area OSPF (Open Shortest Path First) routing using Cisco Packet Tracer.
1. TOPOLOGY
Add these devices: - 3 Routers (1841) - 2 Laptops (Laptop-PT)
Connections:
1. Laptop0 → Router0
2. Router0 → Router1
3. Router1 → Router2
4. Router2 → Laptop1

Area distribution:
- R0 and R1 connection: Area 0
- R1 and R2 connection: Area 1
- R1 acts as an ABR (Area Border Router) because it connects both areas.

3. CONFIGURE LAPTOPS
Laptop0 → Desktop → IP Configuration
IP Address:      192.168.1.2
Subnet Mask:     255.255.255.0
Default Gateway: 192.168.1.1
Laptop1 → Desktop → IP Configuration
IP Address:      192.168.2.2
Subnet Mask:     255.255.255.0
Default Gateway: 192.168.2.1

4. CONFIGURE ROUTER R0
enable
configure terminal
interface fastethernet 0/0
ip address 10.10.10.1 255.255.255.252
no shutdown
exit
interface fastethernet 0/1
ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

5. CONFIGURE ROUTER R1
enable
configure terminal
interface fastethernet 0/0
ip address 10.10.10.2 255.255.255.252
no shutdown
exit
interface fastethernet 0/1
ip address 10.101.10.1 255.255.255.252
no shutdown
exit

6. CONFIGURE ROUTER R2
enable
configure terminal
interface fastethernet 0/0
ip address 10.101.10.2 255.255.255.252
no shutdown
exit
interface fastethernet 0/1
ip address 192.168.2.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit


7. CONFIGURE OSPF PROTOCOL
Configure Router R0
enable
configure terminal
router ospf 24222
network 10.10.10.0 0.0.0.3 area 0
network 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
end

Configure Router R1
enable
configure terminal
router ospf 24222
network 10.10.10.0 0.0.0.3 area 0
network 10.101.10.0 0.0.0.3 area 1
end

Configure Router R2
enable
configure terminal
router ospf 24222
network 10.101.10.2 0.0.0.3 area 1
network 192.168.2.0 0.0.0.255 area 1
end

8. CHECK IP CONNECTIVITY
Check routing table 
show ip route ospf
show ip ospf neighbor

Check connectivity from Laptop0
Open Desktop → Command Prompt.
ping 192.168.2.2
Check connectivity from Laptop1
ping 192.168.1.2

Expected result: Successful ping replies between both laptops.
